# Agent Space — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` for local development: cp .env.example .env
#
# Browser-safe vars are prefixed with VITE_ and are embedded in the WASM/JS bundle
# at build time (Trunk). Never put secrets in VITE_* variables.
#
# Server-only vars stay in InsForge secrets or your local shell — never commit real values.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only — Vapi (Track D)
# Used by edge functions and `vapi listen` for webhook verification.
# Set in InsForge secrets for production; export locally for CLI webhook forwarding.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VAPI_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only — InsForge CLI (Track C)
# Used by `npx @insforge/cli login` and deploy commands. Never expose to the browser.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSFORGE_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only — Nebius Token Factory (Track E, H)
# OpenAI-compatible LLM API key for agent-chat edge function.
# InsForge secrets ONLY — never ship to the client or use in VITE_* vars.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEBIUS_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser-safe — Vapi public key (Track D)
# Embedded at build time; safe to expose in the client bundle.
# Find in the Vapi dashboard under API keys (public / client key).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_VAPI_PUBLIC_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser-safe — InsForge project URL (Track B, G)
# Base URL for room-state polling and edge function requests from the browser.
# Example: https://your-project.insforge.app
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_INSFORGE_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser-safe — InsForge anon key (optional, Track B)
# Only needed if the client calls InsForge directly (e.g. realtime or auth).
# Room-state polling via edge functions typically does not require this.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_INSFORGE_ANON_KEY=
